<& /page/page_title.mas, title=>"<i>Solanum lycopersicoides</i> 基因組聯盟(The <i>Solanum lycopersicoides</i> Genome Consortium)" &>

<& /genomes/Solanum_lycopersicoides/usage_popup.mas &>

<div class="page_introduction">

  <a href="/organism/Solanum%20lycopersicoides/view/"><i>Solanum
  lycopersicoides</i></a> 是一種與栽培番茄 <a href="/organism/Solanum lycopersicum/view"><i>Solanum
  lycopersicum</i></a> 相關的野生番茄物種。(is a wild tomato species 
  related to the domesticated <i>Solanum lycopersicum</i>.)

</div>

<&| /page/info_section.mas, title=>"免責聲明與數據存取協議(Disclaimer and data access agreement)" &>

<div style="text-align: justify; border: 1px solid gray; padding: 2em 3em 3em 3em">

<h3 style="text-align: center"><i>Solanum lycopersicoides</i> 數據存取協議(<i>Solanum lycopersicoides</i> Data Access Agreement)</h3>
<h4 style="text-align: center">在存取 SOLANUM LYCOPERSICOIDES 未公開定序數據前請先閱讀(PLEASE READ BEFORE ACCESSING THE PRE-PUBLICATION SEQUENCE OF SOLANUM LYCOPERSICOIDES)</h4>

<p>
 博伊斯湯普森研究所 (Boyce Thompson Institute) 和亞琛工業大學 (RWTH Aachen University) 很高興公開發布未正式發表的 Solanum lycopersicoides LA2951 基因組序列，作為植物育種和生物學的資源。(The Boyce Thompson Institute and RWTH Aachen University are pleased to make the pre-publication 
 Solanum lycopersicoides LA2951 genome sequences publicly available as a resource for plant breeding and biology.)
</p>

<p>
 透過存取這些數據，本人特此同意根據多倫多協議 (Toronto agreement) 尊重該聯盟在經過同儕審查的刊物中分析並發表首次全域分析的權利。這包括：1) 對基因、基因家族和重複序列的全染色體或全基因組層級分析；以及 2) 與其他生物體的比較分析。不與聯盟計劃重疊的研究可在達成協議後進行。請聯絡 <a href="mailto:usadel@bio1.rwth-aachen.de">Bjorn Usadel 博士(Dr. Bjorn Usadel)</a> 或 <a href="mailto:srs57@cornell.edu">Susan Strickler 博士(Dr. Susan Strickler)</a> 討論此類可能性。(By accessing these data, I hereby agree to respect the rights of the consortium to analyze and 
 publish the first global analyses in a peer-reviewed publication according to the Toronto agreement. 
 This includes: 
 1) whole chromosome or whole genome level analyses on genes, gene families, and repetitive sequences and 
 2) comparative analyses with other organisms. 
 Studies that do not overlap with those planned by the consortium may be undertaken following an agreement. 
 Please contact <a href="mailto:usadel@bio1.rwth-aachen.de">Dr. Bjorn Usadel</a> or <a href="mailto:srs57@cornell.edu">Dr. Susan Strickler</a> 
 to discuss such possibilities.)
</p>

<p>
 所有遵守上述限制的人士均可免費下載和使用這些數據。(The data may be freely downloaded and used by all who respect the restrictions described above.)
 <b>在正式發表之前，對 S. lycopersicoides 基因組數據的任何使用都必須遵守該協議，並必須註明出處為「Solanum lycopersicoides 基因組聯盟」。(Any use of the S. lycopersicoides genome data prior to its publication must follow the agreement 
 and must credit "The Solanum lycopersicoides Genome Consortium".)</b>
</p>

 
</div>  

</&>

<&| /page/info_section.mas, title => '組裝詳情(Assembly details)' &>

<p>
使用 PacBio 技術以 90X 深度對基因組進行定序，並使用 Canu 進行組裝。Contig 使用 Quiver 和 Pilon 進行錯誤校正，並使用 Hi-C 構建 scaffold。使用 PBJelly 配合 PacBio 序列填充缺口。(The genome was sequenced at 90X coverage using PacBio technology and was assembled with Canu. Contigs were error-corrected with Quiver and Pilon and scaffolded with Hi-C. Gaps were filled with PacBio sequence using PBJelly.)
<br><br>
contig 總長度(contig total length): 1,254,763,366 bp<br>
contig 數量(no contigs): 17,507<br>
最長 contig(longest contig): 3,446,189 bp<br>
contig N50: 139,475 bp<br>
<br>
最終組裝總長度(final assembly total length): 1,269,715,057 bp<br>
序列數量(no sequences): 3,096<br>
最終組裝 N50(final assembly N50): 93,894,821 bp<br>
最長序列(longest sequence): 133,820,975 bp<br>
組裝序列的 89.7% 分佈在 12 個 scaffold 中(89.7% of the assembly is found in 12 scaffolds)<br>
</p>

</&>


<&| /page/info_section.mas, title => '註釋詳情(Annotation details)' &>
<p>Augustus 和 snap 經過訓練後作為 Maker 流程中的預測工具。作為輸入的序列數據包括：PacBio IsoSeq、來自葉、果實和花的 RNA-seq、來自 S. lycopersicum、S. pennellii 和 refseq 的蛋白質。共預測了 37,938 個基因，其中 34,240 個位於假分子上。(Augustus and snap were trained to use as predictors in the Maker pipeline. Sequence data used as input includes: PacBio IsoSeq, RNA-seq from leaves, fruit, and flowers, proteins from S. lycopersicum, S. pennellii, and refseq. A total of 37,938 genes were predicted, 34,240 of these are located on pseudomolecules.)</p>

</&>


